# Derived by hand from rulings FB and NO: `==` is bit identity except that every NaN equals every NaN; `^Ord` is the IEEE total order with every NaN one value after +infinity. `nan`, `-nan` and `nan + 1.0` are equal and order Equal; each NaN is Greater than infinity and than -infinity, and not less than 0.0. The map's two keys are distinct; a NaN of other bits finds the NaN key; `-0.0` is not `0.0`, so it is missing. An array of NaN equals one of -NaN; `0.0 == -0.0` is false.
test nan_one

